Cosmology (@cosmology: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_5SVG26YNNHQQ10GHQB7V0YRN48
Cosmology studies the large-scale structure, history, and evolution of the universe. This material connects gravitation, expansion, early-universe processes, background radiation, structure formation, and observational inference, distinguishing established evidence from unresolved questions about the universe's contents and fundamental description.

**Common preparation developed:** the [cosmological distance lesson](../../core/Distinguish-cosmic-redshift-from-local-velocity-and-distance.lingua) distinguishes expansion redshift, look-back time, proper distance and luminosity/angular distances in a declared flat kinematic model. The historical evidence lesson separates inferred distances from independent tests. Full cosmological dynamics, inference and advanced research remain pending.

**Parent:** [Universe and space](../Universe-and-space.lingua#r_38KB376VFZ30BXTGB9K0HG55ZP).
} r_5SVG26YNNHQQ10GHQB7V0YRN48
